<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Nobody misses a dental checkup by deciding to. It just quietly becomes
    three years, because there is no moment at which anything reminds you,
    and the last one is a date nobody wrote down.
  </p>
  <p>
    The radar is the thing that notices. What's due, what's overdue, what's
    already booked — for everyone in the household, including the ones who
    can't tell you they're uncomfortable.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Both halves matter</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "You're due") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The checks that have gone too long, by whatever interval you told it
        — because how often you want an eye test is your business, not a
        guideline the software imported.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "You're booked") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The quiet half. Something on the calendar means the radar stops
        asking and says handled instead — an assistant that can only nag
        adds anxiety rather than removing it.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Everyone it covers</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Health work is rarely only your own. The parent you've started looking
    after, the child whose immunisations you're tracking, the dog whose
    booster is due — all of it produces the same kind of forgetting, and all
    of it lands on one radar rather than in a different app each.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">It doesn't guess intervals</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    The app does not decide how often you ought to see a dentist, and it
    isn't shipping medical guidance disguised as defaults. You say what you
    want tracked and how often; it does the remembering, which is the part
    that was actually failing.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">No model required</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    This is arithmetic on dates. It works on an installation with nothing
    configured, and it is one of the clearest cases of the app being useful
    before it is clever.
  </p>
</section>
